# 7. FLAT-WISE PRIVACY – STRICT REQUIREMENT

**This is a mandatory security condition.**

A resident of Flat 101 must not view private data belonging to Flat 102.

The same rule applies to all flats.

### Authorization rules

- Residents see only their assigned flats.
- All access permissions are validated by the backend.
- Flat IDs must not be trusted merely because the frontend sends them.
- Residents cannot change a URL or API parameter to access another flat.
- Residents cannot browse other residents' contact information.
- Residents cannot download other flats' receipts.
- Residents cannot view other flats' complaints.
- Residents cannot edit financial balances.
- Treasurer and Secretary access is controlled by assigned roles.
- Resident access must be revoked when ownership or occupancy changes.

One user may access multiple flats only when explicitly approved and configured.

### Mandatory test

Log in as Flat 101 and attempt to request Flat 102's:

- Maintenance statement
- Receipts
- Payment records
- Complaints
- Personal details

Every unauthorized request must be denied server-side.

